  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration found is config_045 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy, with config_051 (same encoders, concat) at 0.7207 and config_042 (same encoders, avgpool + weighted) at 0.7062. This establishes a clear hierarchy: transformer > avgpool and weighted ≥ concat for the top encoder pair. Question: config_025 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat) is the last untested cell in the 2×2 aggregation×fusion matrix for the best-performing encoder combination. Testing it completes the matrix and confirms whether the observed monotonic improvements (transformer+weighted > transformer+concat > avgpool+weighted) hold for the remaining combination, or whether there is any unexpected interaction. Why this is the best use: With only 2 experiments remaining, I need to confirm that 0.7250 is indeed the ceiling for this architecture family before spending the final experiment. config_025 is the cheapest remaining test (~4.5–4.8 GPU hours, comparable to config_042 at 4.82) that directly addresses the key uncertainty. It is unlikely to exceed 0.7250 given the consistent ~0.019 transformer-avgpool gap and ~0.004 weighted-concat gap, but confirming this frees the last experiment for a broader architectural exploration (e.g., singleprofile or a different encoder pairing) rather than a redundant confirmation."
